  "question": {
    "html": "<p>An electric motor is used to pull a crate of mass <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"M\"></span> up a frictionless ramp at a constant speed <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"v\"></span>. The ramp is inclined at an angle <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\theta\"></span> to the horizontal. If the motor has an efficiency <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\eta\"></span>, which of the following expressions represents the electrical power input to the motor?</p><ol class=\"mcq-options\"><li data-label=\"A\"><p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{M g v \\sin \\theta}{\\eta}\"></span></p></li><li data-label=\"B\"><p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\eta M g v \\sin \\theta\"></span></p></li><li data-label=\"C\"><p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{M g v \\cos \\theta}{\\eta}\"></span></p></li><li data-label=\"D\"><p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{M g v}{\\eta}\"></span></p></li></ol>"
  },
